s1-p4 = prose (cons "**Process, action, and information.** A state type \(S\), a family of available actions \(A(s)\), and a relation \(T(s,a,s')\) specify an action-labeled transition: a source state, an admitted action, a successor, and evidence of their relation. No state is primitive: there is no primitive thing, only a primitive law of interaction, and a state is determined entirely by its future admissible interactions, which are \(A\) and \(T\) from that state onward. A deterministic update selects its successor; a nondeterministic description retains the admitted alternatives. An open interaction includes the response on which its continuation depends. A policy for selecting an action, the transition relating that action to its consequences, and an observation of those consequences are different constructions. Neither a scalar reward nor a probability distribution is implicit in merely specifying them." nil)
